course: dictionary
lesson: 3428
title: Words that name machines
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words tell you what a thing does, and the ending can give you a clue. Extract means to pull something out. An extractor is the machine or tool that does the pulling out. The ending -or often means "a thing that does this job".
explain: Look at the words around it. «An extractor fan sucks up steam and smoke through a filter.» The words sucks up and steam tell you the job: it takes steam out of the air. So an extractor is something that removes things.
explain: The same word can name different machines. «In late summer the beekeeper slices the wax caps off heavy frames and spins the honey out in a drum called an extractor.» Here the extractor is a drum, not a fan. The words called an extractor tell you it is the name of a special machine.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Try: «The beekeeper spins the honey out in a drum that pulls the honey out.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An extractor is a machine or tool that pulls or takes something out.
fact: An extractor fan removes steam, smoke or smells from a room, such as a kitchen or bathroom.
fact: A honey extractor is a drum that spins honey out of the uncapped cells of a honeycomb.
fact: «Extractor» is a noun, and its plural is «extractors».
fact: «Greasy filters must be cleaned, because the grease can catch fire.»
exercise: «An extractor fan sucks up steam and smoke through a filter.» What does an extractor fan remove? | Cups and plates | Mud from shoes | *Steam and smoke | Sound from the radio
exercise: «In late summer the beekeeper spins the honey out in a drum called an extractor.» What is the extractor in this sentence? | A small fan for the kitchen | A tall hive for bees | A type of wax cap | *A drum that spins honey out
exercise: The ending -or in extractor is a clue. What does it tell you? | A kind of colour | Something that is finished | *A thing that does the action | A place where something lives
test: Which machine is used to get juice out of fruit? | A honey drum | A toaster | A kettle | *A juice extractor
test: «The bathroom extractor stops damp and mould.» Why do bathrooms have an extractor? | To keep the bath warm | To make the water colder | *To remove steam and damp | To play music
exam: What is a splinter extractor? | A kind of plaster | *A tool that takes something out | A fan for steam | A bee's home
